  "projects": [
   {
    "title": "MicroHealth: A Little Goes a Long Way",
    "description": "America, Europe, and even China, are facing an obesity epidemic. Lack of exercise is one major component to this and other critical health problems (e.g., diabetes and cardiovascular disease). When asked why they don't exercise, the majority of people will say they don't have the time to invest into going to the gym. Is there a way to change how people think about daily exercise? \n\nOur solution to the exercise challenge is to break up the amount of exercise one would normally do in a day into smaller fragments so as to make exercising during the day more manageable and less obtrusive. We will facilitate healthy decision making by making these choices routine and easy to perform. An ambient display worn on the users wrist will communicate both their exercise accomplishments as well as new behaviors to perform. We believe through daily, routine micro-exercises one can produce results similar to daily, extensive exercise sessions.",
